3. progression of stats
-------------------------
Physical stats;
Each time a martial arts athletes wrestler trains on a physical stat, he
gains a clear 0.1 point before the modifiers.  Modifiers are his hidden
destiny value (affinity for the given field) in a percentage and an age
coefficient which is calculated by this formula (and later a training focus
modifier):


So each time a martial arts athletes wrestler trains a physical stat sees
an increase:

destiny_value_coefficient = ((destiny_value - (current_value - 20)) / 100)

physical stat increase = point * destiny_value_coefficient * training_coefficient


Skill stats: 
destiny_value_coefficient = ((destiny_value - (current_value - 20)) / 100)
training focus coefficient
physical stat dependence coeffiecient = physical stat / (skill stat + 20)
or if they depend on more than one physical stats: 1 / {number_of_stats} * physical stats / (skill stat + 20)
dependence on multiple stats can be weighted with coefficients, if n coefficients are less than 1, then {new_number_of_stats} = {number_of_stats} - n

skill stat increase = point * destiny_value_coefficient * dependence_coefficient * training_coefficient 


3. destiny value generation
----------------------------
Random with normal distribution

body types may add a small bonus or penalty to certain physical skills


          Agility       Strength        Flexibility         Stamina
==================================================================== 
VSmall |  +0-10          -0-15            +0-10              +0-10 | 
Small  |  +0-5           -0-10            +0-5               +0-5  | 
Light  |   0-0           -0-5              0-0                0-0  |  
Middle |   0-0           +5--5             0-0                0-0  |  
LHeavy |   0-0           +0-5              0-0                0-0  |   
Heavy  |  -0-5           +0-10            -0-5               -0-5  |    
SHeavy |  -0-10          +0-15            -0-10              -0-10 |   
====================================================================


4. training focus
------------------
General training: x1 modifier to everything
Focus on e.g. kicking: x1.5 modifier on kicking, x0.5 modifier on everything else

Focus is applied on one week only, on all three training sessions

Focus will affect martial arts athletes wrestler motivation depending on
their personality. Some sumo wrestlers might like kicking focus, cardio,
or higher intensity training and if you go too
long without their preference they will lose motivation.

Three main categories:
1. Striking
2. Kicking
3. Holds

To implement in the future (only basic focuses and no focus are in the
game): You can upgrade your training focus for more efficient training by
paying some money and taking coach courses. For levels over Advanced you
can only advance through random special events

Striking |  Basic Striking  |   x1.25 striking, x0.75 strength, x0.5 everything else
         |  Inter. Strik.   |   x1.25 striking, x1 strength, x0.5 everything else
         |  Advanced Strik. |   x1.25 striking, x1 strength, x0.75 everything else
         |  Expert Striking |   x1.5 striking, x1 strength, x0.75 everything else
         |  Master Striking |   x1.5 striking, x1.25 strength, x1 everything else
         |  Legendary Str.  |   x2 striking, x1.5 strength, x1 everything else

Kicking  |  Basic Kicking   |   x1.25 kicking, x1 flexibility, x0.5 everything else

Holds    |  Basic Holds     |   x1.25 holds, x0.5 everything else

No Focus: x0.75 to all stats


5. stat history
-----------------
During the first week of every month, all stat increases of the last
training of the week are saved. You can view these later in order to
determine the rate of growth of your martial arts athletes wrestlers. Only
the 60 previous stat increases are saved, meaning stat increases older
than 5 years will be erased.

As of right now, the leftmost value is the oldest one, going to newer values
as one reads to the right. 


6. training preference / motivation / personality
--------------------------------------------------
Motivation shows how happy a martial arts athletes wrestler is with your
dojo. An unmotivated sumo wrestler may leave your dojo soon unless you
make them happier, a highly motivated marital artist will most likely 
stick around. Motivation naturally decreases over time (-2 per week?). 
When a new martial arts athletes wrestler arrives they start with a 
motivation of 50.

You can increase motivation by setting training focus according to your
martial arts athletes wrestlers' training preference. Training preferences 
are:

1. Kicking
2. Dodging
3. Grappling
4. General
5. None 

If e.g. a martial arts athletes wrestler has a training preference for
kicking and they participate in training with kicking focus enabled,
they will gain +5 motivation (can only gain motivation this way once per
week). Students with a general training preference like training with no
focus and martial arts athletes wrestlers with no preference will gain
+0.25 motivation per week regardless.

Right now training preference is generated to be completely random. When
personalities get added, it may be generated by the martial arts athletes
wrestler's personality (depending on what I settle on till then).

Personalities also affect morale
Personalities:

a. Driven: Will get sad if they don't regularly participate in events,
slightly faster stat gain in all stats. Gain morale each time they participate
in an event. Will lose morale if participating in low intensity training and
will gain morale when participating in low intensity training.

b. Impatient: Will get sad if their stats don't improve fast enough. Will
slightly gain morale when participating in high intensity training.

c. Worshipper: Will get sad if you don't have more than 4 black belts in your
dojo, will be really happy otherwise. 

d. Weeb: Will get happy if your dojo has another weeb in it. Everybody else
gets sad for each martial arts athletes wrestler with Weeb personality.

e. Social: Will gain morale for each other martial arts athletes wrestler you have in your
dojo. When relationships are implemented, they will be really happy when they
make friends and really unhappy when disliked.

f. Antisocial: Will lose morale for every social martial arts athletes wrestler you have in your
dojo.

g. Lazy: Massive morale loss if made to participate in events. Slight morale
loss when taking part in high intensity training, morale gain when
participating in low intensity training.

h. Jealous: Loses morale for each martial arts athletes wrestler in the same belt rank that has
better stats.

i. Respectful: Will gain morale for each martial arts athletes wrestler in the same rank that has
better stats (basically the inverse of jealous personality).

j. Unmotivated: Morale loss for high intensity training, slower stat growth

k. Insecure: Will lose morale for each martial arts athletes wrestler who is younger than them.

to implement when relationships are implemented 
l. Troublemaker: will gain morale if people dislike them, will cause trouble
when implemented.

o. Traditionalist: will lose morale if you advertise for new martial arts athletes wrestlers, will gain
morale if there are mentor relationships in the dojo

7. martial arts athletes wrestler belt ranks 
----------------------
a. white belt 
all newcomers start with this belt

b. white / yellow belt 

c. yellow belt

d. yellow / green belt

e. green belt

f. green / blue belt

g. blue belt

h. blue / red belt

i. red belt

j. red / black belt

k. black belt / 1st dan
All skills need to be over 40, at least one needs to be over 50 -this will
be implemented when black belts get a makeover, below these values they 
will generate negative effects for the dojo

A martial arts athletes wrestler can only take a black belt test at least
one year after gaining the red / black belt rank and only in January. That
makes the maximum possible time to take a test for the black belt 1.5
years and the minimum 1 year.

Each time a martial arts athletes wrestler climbs in rank, they get a +10
boost in motivation. An exception to this is gaining the black belt rank,
which gets them +30 motivation.

(below ranks are not implemented yet)
Either hard limits to gain next rank or give the decision to the player
on who to advance to the black belt rank. Black belts will be highly
influential to the dojo's reputation depending on their skill (the higher
the dan rank, the more pronounced the effects) and will also help younger
martial arts athletes wrestlers develop quicker, take on proteges, defend
your dojo's honour against rival dojo attacks, etc. Black belts that aren't
skilled enough will have a big negative impact on your dojo's reputation.
If you choose not to award a martial arts athletes wrestler a black belt,
or delay their advance in rank, their motivation will drop rapidly.

l. black belt / 2nd dan
Any one skill stat over 70, all skill stats over 50
Can take test for 2nd dan only after two years after gaining 1st dan rank.
After 2 years, you can take exam for 2nd dan rank only by having any one
skill stat over 60.

m. black belt / 3rd dan
Any one skill stat over 80, all skill stats over 60
Can take exam three years after gaining 2nd dan rank.
After 3 years, martial arts athletes wrestler can take exam for 3rd dan rank if they have any one
skill over 70 

n. black belt / 4th dan
This test requires the martial arts athletes wrestler to undergo a teaching course. 
Teaching skill over 60, requirements from the 3rd dan still apply.

As the dojo owner, you start out at the 4th dan rank yourself. Therefore you
are only allowed to award up to the 3rd dan rank to your martial arts athletes wrestlers. To award
4th or higher dan ranks you need to up your rank as well by taking a test in
the region's most prestigious dojo. -idea, implement player character as a
special martial arts athletes wrestler? nahh, just have the player pay to get to higher ranks


8. martial arts athletes wrestler leave and new martial artists
----------------------------------
As of now, martial arts athletes wrestlers leave only because of low
morale and there is no difference between new and old martial arts
athletes wrestlers. Students also have a 1/10000 chance to just leave
with no explanation. The rest are all future plans:

The first six months should be very volatile. The six months after that
also, but not as much. New martial arts athletes wrestlers are much harder
to please, negative morale effects are huge and so they may leave at a
moment's notice. After that, it's mostly smooth sailing till the black belt.

Upon gaining the black belt, martial arts athletes wrestlers, depending
on their personality, have a chance of just plain giving up and pursuing
other passions. Even if they do stay, however, black belts are really
tough to handle and touchy and if not kept happy could jump ship at any time.

If the martial arts athletes wrestler's motivation is kept over 85 for
an extended period of time (say two years?), they gain loyalty towards
you, which means that it will be very rare for them to leave, even if
their morale is abysmal. They will never give up upon reaching black belt
status. (maybe some bonus? maybe sumin extra?  maybe give the dojo more
prestige or somethin i dunno)

There is a small possibility that martial arts athletes wrestlers leave
regardless of what you do due to major changes in their life like changing
where they live, a massive injury, having kids etc. It's just the unfair
way life works, I guess.

New martial arts athletes wrestlers will be determined by the dojo's
prestige, but I think a good number is 2-6 new martial arts athletes
wrestlers every year. I should probably not worry about this too much,
though, need to implement martial arts athletes wrestler leave to work
out the numbers well.



9. training intensity -not implemented yet
----------------------
low intensity: x0.75 modifier to all stat gains
medium intensity: x1 modifier to all stat gains
high intensity: x1.25 modifier to all stat gains

Intensity will affect martial arts athletes wrestler motivation depending on
their personality.  High intensity training will also increase martial arts
athletes wrestler fatigue quicker and will increase risk of injury. (fatigue
and injuries not implemented yet).

10. money handling / advertising
---------------------------------
Money makes the world go round.

Each martial arts athletes wrestler pays you 100€ a month. Starting dojo
rent is 500€, and your initial budget is 1000€. If you are in debt
for three months straight, your dojo closes and you go bankrupt, GAME OVER!

/* advertising is not yet implemented
 */
Apart from the standard yearly batch of martial arts athletes wrestlers in September, you can
advertise to get a few martial arts athletes wrestlers immediately. Here the options for advertising:

Posters & flyers locally: 200€, 0-3 martial arts athletes wrestlers next week
Billboards & Newspaper ads: 800€, 0-6 martial arts athletes wrestlers next week
TV & radio ads: 2000€, 2-8 martial arts athletes wrestlers next week

This is the only use for money at the moment
Future uses: participation in events requires a participation fee, the
higher the event rank, the pricier it is to participate. Placing high in
tournaments gives you prize money.


11. events
-----------

This one's gonna be a long one.

Every March, events are held. You can register a martial arts athletes
wrestler of yours to participate in an event during the months
August-December by paying the event's participation fee. (Each event
will contain a stack with the martial arts athletes wrestlers that will
be participating in it).

Events are split into categories by skill: Striking, Kicking, Holds.
They are also split in two difficulty levels: Intermediate and Master.
Radom generated number that has to be over 60 is martial arts athletes
wrestler's performance.

(Events being held in March are temporary, they will be held in different
dates depending on the event, but you will still have to register your
martial arts athletes wrestler months in advance)

Event performance:

xx. command line options
-------------------------

There is one command line option you can pass when running the executable for
debug purposes.

Specifying --happy-times when running the dojo exec file will stop martial
arts athletes wrestlers from leaving your dojo due to morale reasons.


xx. project lateral movement
----------------------------

Transition from this being a general martial arts game to it being a
martial arts athletes game.

Pros:
1. Introduction of decision-making during fights/events, better gameplay
    loop.
2. Solves the problem of how events will play out.
3. Stats make more sense in a rock-paper-scissors type of way.
4. Advanced strategy training adds one more layer in training. 
5. Pre-defined divisions, more clear-cut goals.

Cons:
1. Makes belt ranks obsolete and useless. Not really, black belts are 
    representatives of your dojos and creates a hierarchy with people with
    more and less influence on the dojo. Dojo Reputation is tied to black
    belts, but also black belts may disagree with you. This is tough to 
    implement though and is only a far future implementation.
2. Will have to generate/design hundreds of martial arts athletes wrestlers.
    Or just have most of the tournament rival athletes randomly generated.
3. Will have to figure out how advancing up the ranks works. --what do I 
    mean by this?
4. Will have to rework most of the stats. --nope.


Every athlete has three stats, pushing, grappling, dodging (maybe a stat
for the tachiai?). At the start of a tournament a martial arts athletes
will choose 3 strategies that will have one of their three stats as a
base stat.  Pushing beats grappling, grappling beats dodging and dodging
beats pushing, just like rock paper scissors. Some advanced strategies
may have one base and one secondary stat.

A martial arts athletes chooses between one out of three strategies at
the start of each bout. They don't know what their opponent will choose,
but know their 3 available options. If they are facing them for the first
time, they only know their stats in approximation (let's not do that for 
now). A martial arts athletes
can change their strategy mid-bout, but that will give a penalty to their
physical wear-and-tear and they will receive a slight penalty to their
stats for the rest of the match.

Between each tournament, a martial arts athletes has a chance to train. They
can choose to improve a stat or invest in a new advanced strategy. At
higher divisions, you will only see advanced strategies.

--------------------------------------------------------------

In tournaments, you go up against opponents. There may be 1 or 3 rounds.
In the start of each round, you select one of three stats that function
as rock-paper scissors. Rock gets +10 boost over scissors etc. If you
select the same stat, higher number wins. Opponent stats may have fog of war
applied to them. You can upgrade your scouting by investing money. Low
stamina might incur penalties if you fight many matches in a tournament
or if it goes multiple rounds. If you win a tournament, you advance to
a tougher tournament. Tournaments yield prize money and more popularity
for your gym, meaning more sponsors and more recruits.


Finally I have a clearly defined game loop.
